# Rust — terrain + UI

## Rules

- All terrain is generated in `world/` — never move generation into the UI layer
- Keep determinism: the same (seed, params, x, y) must produce the same result
- Seed is `u64`; profile: `seed % 6`
- UI: `app.rs` (egui). Compose: `render.rs`. Settlements/roads: `settlements_draw.rs`. Ecology wash: `ecology_draw.rs`. Biome colors: `colors.rs`
- Params: `TerrainGenParams` → `apply_to(&mut WorldConfig)`

## Code conventions

- Use `rayon` for parallel grid generation
- Noise helpers live in `world/noise.rs` — do not duplicate them
- Add new biomes in `world/biome.rs`, colors in `colors.rs`
- Add new shape profiles in `world/shape.rs` and update `from_index` (`% N`)
- Heavy generation runs on a worker thread; do not block the egui frame

## world module layout

```
world/
  config.rs     — WorldConfig, LOD, ShapeProfile, TerrainGenParams
  types.rs      — TileType, TerrainCell, TerrainGrid, RegionId, ChunkId
  prng.rs       — hash / derive from u64 seed
  noise.rs      — fBm, clamp, lerp, redistribution
  shape.rs      — 6 land-shape profiles
  elevation.rs  — relief belts / orogeny
  ridge.rs      — ridges
  biome.rs      — biome classification
  sampler.rs    — main terrain sampler
  grid.rs       — generate_global / region / chunk / view
  river.rs      — river network
  settlement.rs — settlements + roads
  ecology.rs    — region/chunk habitat + life
  delta.rs      — stub for future terrain edits
```
